values ('ap_precalculus', 3, '3.3', array['3.3']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Exact first-quadrant values of cosine and sine', 'Exact values come from isosceles right and equilateral triangles for multiples of pi/4 and pi/6; use the quadrant to set the sign.', '[{"label": "\\pi/6", "meaning": "\\cos=\\sqrt{3}/2,\\ \\sin=1/2"}, {"label": "\\pi/4", "meaning": "\\cos=\\sqrt{2}/2,\\ \\sin=\\sqrt{2}/2"}, {"label": "\\pi/3", "meaning": "\\cos=1/2,\\ \\sin=\\sqrt{3}/2"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'These are reference values for the first quadrant. For terminal rays in other quadrants, use the same magnitudes and attend to the signs.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-precalculus-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_precalculus-u3-r1-010; ced=3.3.A.2 "exact values for the cosine and sine of angles that are multiples of π/4 and π/6"')
