values ('ap_precalculus', 3, '3.6', array['3.6', '3.7']::text[], 'formula', 'Converting frequency to the parameter b', '|b|=2\pi\cdot\text{frequency},\qquad \text{since } \text{period}=\frac{2\pi}{|b|}\ \text{and}\ \text{frequency}=\frac{1}{\text{period}}', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'The relationship fixes the magnitude of b: a frequency of 200 cycles per second gives |b| = 400 pi, and b may be negative with the same period and frequency (3.6.A.1 permits any nonzero real b). Do not set b equal to the frequency or to the period.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-precalculus-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_precalculus-u3-r3-003; ced=3.5.A.2 "period and frequency ... are reciprocals" with 3.6.A.6 "a period of (1/b)2π units"; used in 3.7.A.1; product-owner-directed correction by the Claude session (David, 2026-10-10): the escalated row was corrected against its own CED evidence and re-checked by both independent checkers and the own-family veto')
