values ('ap_precalculus', 3, '3.6', array['3.6', '3.7']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Reading a, b, c, d in a sinusoidal function', 'Characteristics of y = a sin(b(θ + c)) + d (same for cosine), with the transformation each parameter causes.', '[{"label": "Amplitude", "meaning": "|a|; vertical dilation of the graph by a factor of |a|"}, {"label": "Period", "meaning": "\\frac{1}{|b|}\\cdot 2\\pi=\\frac{2\\pi}{|b|}; horizontal dilation by a factor of 1/|b|"}, {"label": "Midline / vertical shift", "meaning": "d units from y = 0, so the midline is y = d"}, {"label": "Phase shift", "meaning": "-c units (horizontal translation)"}]'::jsonb, NULL, 'The phase shift is -c, the opposite sign of c, and it applies only when the form is b(θ + c), with b factored out.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-precalculus-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_precalculus-u3-r1-020; ced=3.6.A.6 "amplitude of |a| units, a period of (1/|b|)2π units, a midline vertical shift of d units ... phase shift of −c units"')
