values ('ap_precalculus', 3, '3.7', array['3.7']::text[], 'list_sequence', 'Building a sinusoidal model from data', 'Key values of a sinusoidal model are estimated from period, extreme values, and a matching input-output pair, or found with technology.', '[{"label": "Period and frequency", "meaning": "Use the input-value interval between consecutive maxima or consecutive minima (3.7.A.1)."}, {"label": "Amplitude and vertical shift", "meaning": "Use the maximum and minimum output values. The amplitude is half their difference and the midline is their average (3.7.A.2, 3.5.A.3, 3.5.A.4)."}, {"label": "Phase shift", "meaning": "Compare an actual input-output pair with pairs produced by the model (3.7.A.3)."}, {"label": "Technology", "meaning": "Estimate key values or use sinusoidal regression for a data set (3.7.A.4)."}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-precalculus-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_precalculus-u3-r2-005; ced=3.7.A.1–3.7.A.4: "consecutive maxima or consecutive minima"; "sinusoidal regressions"')
