values ('ap_precalculus', 3, '3.10', array['3.10', '3.12']::text[], 'convention', 'Solving trigonometric equations and inequalities', 'Inverse trig functions help solve trig equations and inequalities, but because trig functions are periodic there are often infinitely many solutions, and the inverse''s output may need to be modified for the domain restriction.', '[]'::jsonb, NULL, 'A single inverse-trig output is only one solution. Find the other solutions and check them against the stated or contextual domain.', 'published', 'generated-checked; extractor=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5; batch=ap-precalculus-reference-u1-u3-2026-10-10; candidate=ap_precalculus-u3-r1-029; ced=3.10.A.1-3.10.A.2 "infinitely many solutions to trigonometric equations"')
